        "items": [
          "A clinic website in the UK costs **£3,500 to £12,000+** in 2026. The number tracks systems, not design.",
          "**Core clinic website:** from £3,500 (up to 8 pages, online booking, practitioner directory, price list) — 4 weeks",
          "**Extended:** from £6,500 (+ blog and SEO pages, insurance integration, clinic CRM) — 6 weeks",
          "**Multi-site group:** from £12,000 (multi-location structure, full CRM integration, multilingual) — 8–10 weeks",
          "A one-page brochure site without booking — from £800, but for a clinic it's a stopgap",
          "At Code-Site.Art the sum is fixed in the contract before work starts."
        ],
        "title": "In 60 seconds"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03d",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03e",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Why a clinic website costs more than “just a website”"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03g",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "A practice owner googling “how much does a website cost” sees numbers from £300 to £15,000 — with nothing explaining the gap. The difference isn't design. A clinic website is four systems a regular corporate site doesn't have."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03j",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03h",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ],
            "text": "1. Online booking that actually works. "
          },
          {
            "_key": "cw03i",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "A large share of booking calls land outside opening hours — and go nowhere. A “leave your number” form doesn't fix it: younger patients don't want phone calls at all. Working online booking means picking a service, a practitioner and a time slot in 2 clicks, an SMS confirmation for the patient and a notification for reception. In the quote, that's an integration with your practice management system or CRM — £200 to £500 each."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03m",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03k",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ],
            "text": "2. A practitioner directory with schedules. "
          },
          {
            "_key": "cw03l",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Patients don't book “the clinic” — they book a person. Cards with photos, credentials, specialisms and a live schedule are a separate data structure in the CMS, one your practice manager updates without a developer."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03p",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03n",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ],
            "text": "3. A transparent price list that's easy to update. "
          },
          {
            "_key": "cw03o",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Clinics that hide prices lose patients at the comparison stage: opacity reads as “expensive”. A structured price list managed from the CMS — your marketer updates fees in 2 minutes."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03s",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03q",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ],
            "text": "4. Compliance. "
          },
          {
            "_key": "cw03r",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "CQC expectations, GMC/GDC advertising guidance, UK GDPR consent for patient data. Not a checkbox — incorrectly handled medical websites draw real regulatory attention."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cw03t",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cw03u",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Everything else — design, build quality, speed, local SEO — is the same as any good website. But those four systems add £1,500–3,000 versus a regular corporate site. That's why a “£500 website” and a clinic website are different products."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
